title DAHL-J10r2 — skate_group_signed, a vote that cannot be fabricated
prompt keep going the 1,024-round itinerary; next agent-doable lap, send each increment as its own signed round
think r1 fixed the quorum rule as a pure state machine, yet a bare state machine trusts whoever calls it — a steward could cast a vote in a member's name. r2's crux: bind each vote to the voting member's settled Kumara identity, mirroring skate_circle_signed (r2 of J9).
think Read skate_circle_signed.rye for the exact idiom — a tagged fixed-length message (tag · group_id · voter · candidate = 13 bytes), a bounded Keyring point→key, a verify_over helper, and a *_signed entry that verifies before touching r1. Kept verify_vote touching no group (the verification half alone), so r3's traveled record can re-check a vote offline with no state to mutate — exactly as J9r3 needed verify_join/verify_request split out.
think Design decision on founders: the founders are the group's seeded bootstrap (its genesis); every admission after takes signed distinct votes. Signing the votes is the load-bearing act for the quorum crux — a vote is the consent that must not be fabricated. Documented plainly rather than signing the genesis roster, which would add ceremony without touching the crux.
think Two cruxes proven together: (1) the honesty crux — relabel a vote's candidate after signing and reuse the sig → BadConsent, tally(cate)==0; (2) the lone-steward guard carries through signing — a valid signature lets a member vote once, the repeat refusing AlreadyVoted with tally held at one, so signing cannot fake a quorum from one hand. Also forged-by-wrong-keeper, unknown-keeper (a real member unenrolled), and cross-group each refuse.
obs GREEN first run — no TAME/width fix needed this round (the compound-assert lesson from r1 carried forward; wrote asserts split from the start). Rung one re-runs GREEN under the witness, confirming additivity.
loom witness=dahl_j10_skate_group_signed_witness cases=6 msg_bytes=13 result=GREEN
file pond/apps/skate_group_signed.rye r2 — each vote signed by its member's Kumara identity over (tag · group id · voter · candidate); verify before touching r1's group
